## 2. Run-wide architecture decisions

- **D1. One provenance concept for definitions.** Rename `ReplacementOrigin` to `DefinitionOrigin` (same variants: `Characteristic` as default, and `Resolution`) and generalize its doc to say what it means for both kinds. `Resolution` means a continuous effect generated by resolution (CR 611.2) that is stored on the object and is not one of its abilities (CR 611.2c, CR 613.1f). The carry-across-the-reset semantics stay documented on the replacement side. `StaticDefinition` gains `origin: DefinitionOrigin` with the replacement field's serde attributes (`default`, `skip_serializing_if = is_characteristic`) and an `is_resolution_installed()` predicate.
  - *Reason:* it is one CR 611.2 fact about two definition kinds. A second enum would proliferate. Reusing the replacement-specific name on statics would misname the concept. Variant names, not type names, go on the wire, so the rename is wire-identical; the phase 2 plan establishes the full reference set.
  - *Rejected:* a `StaticOrigin` sibling enum; a `bool`.
- **D2. Single authority: layer 6 in `crates/engine/src/game/layers.rs`.**
  - The graft arms (`AddStaticMode`, `GrantStaticAbility`) decide each grafted static's origin.
  - The `RemoveAllAbilities` arm replaces the clear of statics with a retain of `is_resolution_installed()` statics, mirroring the replacement retain beside it.
  - Combat restriction consumers are **not** edited, and no per-mode TCE-read is added.
  - *Reason:* the draft traced every restriction consumer to grafted `static_definitions`. One retain fixes them all, while a TCE-read per mode would mean N authorities. The phase 2 plan establishes the trace, including that no ability-suppression path (`abilities_suppressed`, `functioning_abilities`) hides a retained graft.
- **D3. The origin derivation rule at graft time.** A grafted static is `Resolution` iff the active effect is resolution-generated (`transient_id.is_some()`) **and** one of these holds:
  - the modification is `AddStaticMode`; or
  - it is `GrantStaticAbility` whose inner definition declares `Resolution`.

  A graft from a non-transient effect is always `Characteristic`, whatever the inner definition declares. This is fail-closed: ability removal still removes it.
  - *Reason:* it keeps CR 611.2 (resolution) separate from CR 611.3 (static ability), and leaves the static-ability-sourced graft path behaviorally unchanged (Psychic Paper deferral, §7). It also means a mis-tagged parser definition on a printed static cannot become irremovable.
  - The phase 2 plan establishes that every transient-sourced active effect comes from a resolving spell or ability. If some other producer sets `transient_id`, that is drift on D3.
- **D4. Representation: a quoted static grant is a granted ability (phase 1).**
  - `parse_quoted_rule_static_modifications` always lowers to `GrantStaticAbility`, carrying the whole parsed quoted definition. The trivial-SelfRef collapse to `AddStaticMode` ends (CR 113.10, CR 113.3d). After phase 1, an `AddStaticMode` from a resolving effect always states a rule effect.
  - **Base collapse predicate** (named because two clauses below use it): `affected == SelfRef`, no `condition`, empty `modifications`; no other field is consulted. At base the collapse kept only `mode` and discarded every other field of the quoted definition (charter review measured, `grammar.rs` ~1773).
  - The perpetual `TryFrom<ContinuousModification> for PerpetualGrantModification` maps a `GrantStaticAbility` that meets the base collapse predicate exactly to the perpetual `AddStaticMode { mode }`, and keeps rejecting every other `GrantStaticAbility`. The perpetual path is therefore unchanged, and it stays fail-closed.
  - On the layer path, the `GrantStaticAbility` graft installs the full quoted definition. A quoted card whose definition carries a field the base collapse discarded can therefore change reading in phase 1, and its reading follows its verbatim Oracle text (Phase 1 Goal).
  - Every reader other than the layer-6 graft arms themselves, in `layers.rs` or elsewhere, that pattern-matches `AddStaticMode{mode}` for a mode in phase 1's regenerated diff reads a `GrantStaticAbility` that meets the base collapse predicate the same way, or records a one-line reason.
  - *Anchors (draft Q7):* the `GrantStaticAbility` arm does **not** copy the `AddStaticMode`-only installer anchors (source controller, chosen color, source object, bound actor) onto quoted definitions. A quoted card the census finds depending on one gets its reading derived from its Oracle text and CR 109.5 (a static ability's "you" is the controller of the object it's on). The phase asserts that derived reading and records an addendum. A general audit is deferred (§7).
  - *Rejected:* putting the marker on the rule-effect side, which would touch the ~766 bare producers; a new `ContinuousModification` variant for rule statics, which would proliferate; keeping the collapse for the predicate-meeting subset on the layer path, which would leave a quoted grant and a rule effect identical on exactly the shape D3 keys on.
- **D5. Non-quoted rule-effect vehicles declare their origin (phase 3).**
  - Every non-quoted resolving-effect producer that rides `GrantStaticAbility` builds its inner definition through one builder, `StaticDefinition::resolution_installed()` in `phase-ast`. Producers include the Promise class, combat tax, temporary cost modification, and graveyard-permission and flash grants. That covers parser producers and engine-side `GenericEffect` synthesizers alike.
  - The stacked Immortal Obligation PR uses the same builder.
  - *Reason:* only the producer knows that a non-quoted `GrantStaticAbility` is a rule effect. The `GrantStaticAbility` shape is what the per-recipient CR 109.5 "you" slot needs.
- **D6. `object_has_no_abilities` ignores `Resolution`-origin statics (draft Q4), phase 2.** Its treatment of replacement definitions is unchanged in this run (§7).
  - *Reason:* D2 requires it. Without it, D2's retain would introduce a regression: a vanilla Grizzly Bears hit by Panic under Dress Down would keep a static and lose Muraganda Petroglyphs' +2/+2. Being required by D2, it is part of unit U1, not a unit of its own.
- **D7. Consumers left unchanged (AC3 sibling census).** The phase 2 plan's census gives each of these a one-line reason:
  - goad (`goading_players_for_creature_gated`);
  - the CantBeTargeted / CantBeCountered / opponent-relative CantBeBlockedBy transient reads;
  - the CantUntap / CantPhaseIn transient scans;
  - suspected-derived abilities;
  - `set_land_subtype_replacing`;
  - text substitution;
  - the AddStaticMode dedup (its equality now includes `origin`).

  Goad stays preserved.
- **D8. Phase order: U3 → U1 → U2.**
  - U1 without U3 makes the quoted class (Craterous Stomp, Incite Hysteria) survive ability removal, which is wrong behavior. So U3 must land first, and no seam exists with U1 first.
  - U2 needs U1's field and retain.
  - U3 and U1 together would be a 2-unit phase of ≥13 paths, which trips T1∧T2. So they are separate phases.
- **D9. Shipping: one commit (at least) per phase on branch `engine/resolved-restrictions-survive-ability-removal`; the PR grouping is Jakob's call, made at run-level acceptance.** He accepted "3 steps, 2-3 PRs" (Command Zone #222) after choosing (#213) that this ships as its own engine PR ahead of #9608. Every phase boundary is a green-tree seam and a valid PR boundary. Candidate groupings: {P1+P2, P3}: P1+P2 delivers AC1/AC2 for the `AddStaticMode` class, and P3 lands the vehicle builder the stacked Immortal Obligation PR needs. Or {P1, P2, P3}. The stacked PR (#9608) rebases onto the last of them. Build-backed verification and the parse-diff measurement stay run-level (base to final) under Step 5. Changing the grouping is never a re-charter.

