## 6. Recursive phase-fit check, and re-charter triggers

- Each phase is one unit (T1 false), so no phase trips T1∧T2 whatever its path count:
  - Phase 1 is U3. Its reading changes (Goal) are consequences of the same representation change, read through existing consumers; they are not a second unit.
  - Phase 2 is U1. D6 is the statics conjunct only, which D2's retain requires (the Grizzly Bears / Muraganda Petroglyphs witness), so it sits inside U1. The replacement conjunct, which would have been a separately tested unit with its own base defect, is out of the run (§7). Phase 2's compiler-forced literal sites may push its T2 count to ≥13. That is expected and harmless at one unit.
  - Phase 3 is U2.
- If a phase plan's Sizing reports ≥2 units with ≥13 paths, that is a second-level firing inside a split phase. It stops for reassessment (chartered.md); it does not re-charter silently.
- **Breaks that require a re-charter:**
  - phase 1's P1 measurement refutes the identical-payload premise (D4);
  - a reading-change card the phase 1 Goal names needs a consumer change that is a unit of its own, outside phase 1's scope rule (D4);
  - `transient_id` turns out to mark non-resolution effects in a way the D3 rule cannot absorb;
  - a retained graft is hidden by a second suppression authority that needs its own design (D2);
  - a quoted card needs an installer anchor that `GrantStaticAbility` cannot carry without a new seam (D4 anchors clause).

  Smaller drift is an addendum.

## 7. Deferrals out of the run (follow-ups; one-line reasons)

- **Psychic Paper (Command Zone #282), restrictions grafted by a printed static ability.** These are CR 611.3 effects of a static ability, not resolution effects. Covering them needs a non-`Resolution` provenance value and its own census of static-line graft producers (Aura/Equipment "enchanted/equipped creature can't …"). D3 leaves that path unchanged, and no test pins its outcome. D1's enum is the extension point.
- **`object_has_no_abilities` counting resolution-installed replacements (moved out of D6, charter review r1 F2).** Pre-existing: it reproduces at base independent of this change (`object_has_no_abilities` counts resolution-installed replacements); no acceptance row depends on it. Witness: Maze of Ith's resolved prevention shield on an attacking Grizzly Bears under Muraganda Petroglyphs. The orchestrator triages it once as a Pre-existing report (file or drop).
- **Frozen affected-set rulings for broadcast rule effects (CR 611.2c, second-to-last sentence; Magmatic Chasm, Falter class).** This is a separate pre-existing defect in how a resolution rule effect's affected set is bound, independent of ability removal. No acceptance row depends on it.
- **CR 109.5 binding of "you" inside quoted grants.** After phase 1, quoted statics no longer receive `AddStaticMode` installer anchors. A general audit of controller-relative quoted text is a separate class. Phase 1 handles only the cards its census finds dependent (D4).

